A||||6||MooCow||Should I move my car out?||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||11-02-2001||10:50 PM||||Well my car is in the shed and it smells so musty it gross. Also cob webs are everywhere and inside my car.  Plus the shed has a moisture problem.  I think I am going to move it out of the shed and put on the side of the house for winter under a car cover.  This way I will be able to start it in the winter, plus I can work on the suspension until winter comes.  The car cant be driven cause there is about an 8 inch crack in the tranny block.  Is there any damage that will come if I do drive it to the side of the house??  I don't need the tranny as I have another one, but I can't push the car cause its on an incline.  Think this is a good idea for me to move it?<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forum_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||11-03-2001||12:10 AM||||Besides flying shrapnel, the only thing that could get hurt using the broken tranny is maybe your speed sensor and gear.  You might get some funny metal shavings if the case rubs on the clutch/flywheel..but it should be alright for a real short trip, not much running time...right?  What does everybody else think?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||11-03-2001||12:26 AM||||Yea I am only moving it about 15 feet but wont be able to push it cause there is a speed bumb type cement that it has to get over in order to make it out of the shed.  It took 3 of us just to get it in there and it was a very tight fit.  Once I move it thought it is staying there all winter.  Also this way I will be able to start it up.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||11-03-2001||02:10 PM||||Why move it/store it in the first place??<P>Oh, that's right. You get some seriously nasty winters in that part of the U.S. of A don't you?<P>I think it will be fine under a good quality car cover during the winter.<BR>Best of luck man.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||11-03-2001||02:50 PM||||If you can't push it up this incline, I'm wondering how the tranny would "hold up" getting up it. I'd be real careful when doing this. Is there any way you can pull it with a truck or something?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||11-03-2001||06:07 PM||||Well I drove the car just fine out of the shed and to its finally resting place till next spring.  The car ran perfect and the tranny held up.  I looked at my extra tranny and then looked where it was cracked at on mine and it runs fine and all but no tranny fluid.  Is it even possible for me to drive the car with the 8 inch crack in the tranny case??  What all will it harm??  I have no use at all for the tranny since I have another one.  I highly doubt I will be able to drive it but really just wish I could.<P>Thanks Everyone, Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forum_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||avengador1||11-03-2001||06:44 PM||||Keep mothballs in the car. They will get rid of the musty smell and hopefully prevent rodents from taking up residence in it. The previous owner of my car kept it outside under a car cover and a field mouse made a home in the left tail light. Luckyly he had moved out by the time I purchased the car and only did some damage to the insulation in the engine compartment ( which I removed anyway). It sure was messy to clean up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
